-----------------------------------------------
- Procedural vs. Object Oriented Programming -
-----------------------------------------------

An object-oriented program is: Object oriented program design is focused on determining, designing and implementing 
a collection of objects that know things and do things.

Procedural Programming
	Where we Identify, Design, Write, Call -> Functions (Fouce on the Functions)

A Program
	is a Package of Responsibilities
		Things to Know (Variables)
		Things it deos (Functions)

Object Oriented Programmming (Collections of Objects)
	For Large Projects like Mircosoft PowerPoint
	We do this by Identify, Desgin, Create Objects (Classes)
	Objects are the packages of responsibility
	Objects Know things and Do things through the Variables and Functions

